-- chem/sectors.hypercubical — every flux sector of a vertex reaches the same innermost labels. chem/magloop.hypercubical
-- proves that the loops of Thiemann's magnetic operator leave the flux between vertices (`beyonds`) unchanged, so
-- that flux labels sectors. chem/electric.hypercubical's energy at the vertex (`electric-terms`) is a function of the
-- labels at the vertex, the innermost ones. Here: from any labels on four ends, a word of loops (`sc-word`) carries
-- the innermost labels to (q, 0, 0, 0), q the charge at the vertex (the labels' sum), with the flux between vertices
-- as it was (`sc-all`, every label from −2 to 2 on each of four ends, 625 sectors). After that word the innermost
-- labels, and so the electric term and every further loop's effect on them, are the same in every sector of the same
-- charge: what a sector's states below that word can do does not depend on the flux between vertices. In this
-- operator the energy at a vertex is a function of the charge at that vertex, and a line of flux of any length
-- between two charges adds nothing: the electric and magnetic terms as regularized in QSD V carry no force between
-- charges at different vertices. A leaf: no module imports it.
import "magloop.hypercubical"

